   {
    "heading": "Follow the reads. Watch every view update.",
    "text": [
     "A classroom example: a short plasmid from a made-up organism is sequenced, the reads are aligned, one read carries an inserted stretch, and the class asks where it came from and whether it keeps the reading frame. Every panel on this page is driven by the same steps; nothing here is measured data."
