      },
      {
       "id": "filter",
       "edge": "finder->filter",
       "text": "**Keep only inserts long enough to trust.** Short inserts can match the reference by chance. The class keeps inserts of 11 letters or more, then requires at most one mismatch to the proposed origin.",
       "panels": {
        "counts": {
         "counts": {
          "long": 3140,
          "confident": 1890
         },
         "active": null,
         "note": "Illustrative counts. 1,890 inserts remain for the frame and junction questions."
        }
       }
      },
      {
       "id": "frame",
       "nodes": [
        "filter"
       ],
       "text": "**Does the insert keep the reading frame?** Twelve is a multiple of three, so the codons after the insert are unchanged and the gene still ends at its own stop. Frame 1 is emphasised; frames 2 and 3 are dimmed for comparison.",
       "panels": {
        "orf": {
         "note": "Twelve letters add four codons (G H C N). Frame 1 keeps its reading and still ends at the gene's own stop."
        },
        "orf13": {
         "note": "Compare with panel A: one extra letter is all that separates the two products."
        }
       }
      },
      {
       "id": "junction",
       "edge": "filter->report",
       "text": "**Which letters sit at the cut?** For every confident insert the class reads the two letters where the inserted stretch was cut from its origin, in a treated and a control sample, and tallies them. One pair stands out in the treated sample only.",
       "panels": {
        "tally": {
         "cells": {
          "treated.ua": 1.6,
          "treated.ug": 1.1,
          "treated.uu": 1.4,
          "treated.ca": -0.2,
          "control.ua": 0.1,
          "control.ug": -0.1,
          "control.uu": 0.2,
          "control.ca": 0.0
         },
         "marks": {
          "treated.ua": "***",
          "treated.ug": "**",
          "treated.uu": "**",
          "control.ua": "ns"
         },
         "highlight": {
          "row": "treated"
         },
         "note": "Illustrative values. Stars mark pairs that pass a multiple-testing threshold in the treated sample."
        }
       }
      },
      {
       "id": "shift",
       "nodes": [
        "filter"
       ],
       "text": "**Alternate ending: a 13-letter insert.** One extra letter shifts every codon that follows. In frame 1 the gene's stop codon is no longer in frame, so the protein would run on past the gene end with the wrong amino acids.",
       "panels": {
        "orf13": {
         "note": "Thirteen letters shift every codon after the insert. The gene's stop is no longer read in frame 1, so translation would run past the gene end."
        },
        "ref": {
         "marks": [
          {
           "id": "site",
           "from": 2430,
           "to": 2431,
           "tone": "bad",
           "label": "13 letters inserted here"
          }
         ]
        },
        "orf": {
         "note": "Panel A stays in frame; panel B is the shifted product this path follows."
        }
       }
      },
      {
       "id": "shift-report",
       "edge": "filter->report",
       "text": "**Report the frameshift.** The class records the insert as frame-breaking. Junction letters are still tallied; the frame question and the junction question are independent.",
       "panels": {
